# Shell scripts MUST be stored and checked out with LF.
#
# This is not a style preference. `entrypoint.sh` is the container entrypoint,
# and a CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter literally named
# "/bin/sh\r", which fails as `bad interpreter: no such file or directory` —
# an error that names the shell and not the line ending, and so reads like a
# broken image rather than a broken checkout.
#
# This was not hypothetical: the first source export of this service to the
# build host carried `#!/bin/sh\r\n` and would have produced exactly that.
*.sh text eol=lf

# The migration is applied by piping it into psql over ssh. Stray carriage
# returns end up inside SQL identifiers and string literals.
*.sql text eol=lf
